      "body": "## Overview\n\nExtend `tests/utils_/test_collection_utils.py` (which previously covered only `is_list_of_numbers`, `common_prefix`, and `swap_dict_values`) with tests for `as_list`, `chunk_list`, `full_groupby`, and `LazyDict`, which had no tests anywhere in `tests/`.\n\n## Claims\n\n- 12 new cases, including the `full_groupby` distinction that motivates the helper (non-contiguous values group together, unlike `itertools.groupby`) and `LazyDict` lazy evaluation, caching, and `KeyError` behavior.\n- CPU-only, no GPU, no downloads.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `pytest tests/utils_/test_collection_utils.py -v` locally: 33 passed (21 pre-existing + 12 new).\n- `ruff check` and `ruff format --check` clean.\n- Also verified via the standard path (real `vllm` import chain and repo conftest, no stubbing, no `--noconftest`): 33 passed.\n\nAI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\nThis PR is not duplicating an existing PR: open PRs were searched for the covered area keywords on Oct 30, 2026, with no matches.",
